    "      \"limits\": [\n",
    "        \"Storage only. Core validates the physical container and the manifest once and returns exact bytes. It does not interpret, deserialize or execute a member, and it needs no Methods library. Readable never implies executable: the inspect view reports executability as not_evaluated and unknown owners stay opaque.\",\n",
    "        \"Source support and qualification are stated separately. Supported means the entrypoint exists in the host source, which is not parity. Executed evidence is stated separately and names the actual host, operation, artifact and platform. The storage route returns bytes and does not evaluate them, and nothing here qualifies a host numerical model, browser use at the full size budget or Windows command quoting.\",\n",
    "        \"Core derives member sizes and raw SHA-256 values and re-serializes the manifest from its typed form. Owner identities, owner strings and reference artifacts are neither authenticated nor fetched. A member replaced by update can leave an owner fingerprint stale; DAG-owned mismatches are reported by the inspect view, foreign ones stay unverified.\",\n",
    "        \"An update always produces a new container with a new digest and never modifies its base. Omitting a member from the new manifest deletes it; there is no tombstone and no in-place append.\",\n",
    "        \"Executing, predicting with or retraining a stored host model is a decision of its owner or the SDK outside Core. Closed native-produced models keep their actions under native-n4a-canonical, and a container mixing native and foreign models stays readable but is refused by those actions.\",\n",
    "        \"The profile id and version, the container schema nirs4all.n4a.container.v1, owner schemas, the Methods ABI and wire format, the recipe language and the package releases are independent compatibility dimensions; none implies another.\",\n",
    "        \"Container content has no intrinsic cap: the zip-stored.v1 profile uses ZIP64 exactly where a value requires it, and only an optional working-memory budget, allocator failure, ZIP and host representation limits and integrity checks refuse. This is source support, not a huge-file, Windows, browser or MATLAB qualification.\",\n",
    "        \"R is an external federation owned by nirs4all-r over the n4a-write, n4a-read and n4a-inspect CLI commands; it is not a Core runtime surface.\"\n",
    "      ]\n",
    "    }\n",
